---
// /docs/memory — Memory, the moat. Pure composition: Base → DocsNav(current="memory")
// → DocSection header → DocDiagram(memory.png) → prose. Facts verbatim from the content map.
// The diagram (diagrams/memory.png) is the copied asset (T1).
//
// Base-path rule (#1 404 trap): DocDiagram takes a BARE path, prefixed via withBase().
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import DocsNav from "../../components/DocsNav.astro";
import DocSection from "../../components/DocSection.astro";
import DocDiagram from "../../components/DocDiagram.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Memory — Agentry Docs"
  description="Memory is Agentry's durable fact/episode store — a local stdio MCP over node:sqlite with project and global roots. It is the moat: each run starts warmer than the last."
>
  <DocsNav current="memory" />

  <DocSection
    eyebrow="Concept · Memory"
    title="Memory — the moat"
    lede="Memory is the durable store that lets a run remember. It graduates a run's lessons into recallable facts, so the next task starts warmer than the last — the compounding advantage Agentry is built around."
  >
    <DocDiagram
      src="diagrams/memory.png"
      alt="Diagram of Memory: a durable fact and episode store backed by node:sqlite, accessed as a local stdio MCP, with a project root and a global root."
      caption="A durable fact/episode store — a local stdio MCP over node:sqlite, with project + global roots."
    />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Memory is a <strong>durable fact/episode store</strong>: it keeps both the semantic facts a
        project accumulates (conventions, gotchas, decisions) and the episodes a run produces, with the
        provenance that earned them. It is exposed as a <strong>local stdio MCP over
        <code>node:sqlite</code></strong> — no network service, no external database; it runs on your
        machine and stores on your disk.
      </p>
      <p>
        Recall is rooted in two scopes. A <strong>project root</strong> holds what is true for
        <em>this</em> repository; a <strong>global root</strong> holds what is true across all your work.
        A task pulls from both, so a lesson learned once is available everywhere it applies.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is <strong>the moat</strong>. Capability you can buy; a store of what <em>your</em> work has
        already taught the system, you can only accumulate — and it compounds with every run.
      </p>
    </div>
  </DocSection>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .prose p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .prose em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
